%% §21 machine 1 of 8 — Athlete Application  (Prisma enum: AthleteState)
%% §21: DRAFT -> SUBMITTED -> UNDER_REVIEW -> APPROVED / CHANGES_REQUESTED / REJECTED -> ACTIVE / SUSPENDED
%% One of the two machines §38 names explicitly. Built by P3-* (B1 · onboarding).
    direction TB
    [*] --> DRAFT : athlete starts application
    DRAFT --> SUBMITTED : submits
    SUBMITTED --> UNDER_REVIEW : network manager picks it up
    UNDER_REVIEW --> APPROVED : accepted into the network
    UNDER_REVIEW --> CHANGES_REQUESTED : more information needed
    UNDER_REVIEW --> REJECTED : declined
    CHANGES_REQUESTED --> SUBMITTED : resubmits (derived)
    APPROVED --> ACTIVE : agreements accepted, profile live
    ACTIVE --> SUSPENDED : conduct / eligibility hold
    SUSPENDED --> ACTIVE : hold lifted (derived)
    REJECTED --> [*]

    note right of APPROVED
      A minor cannot reach ACTIVE until a
      verified guardian is recorded (§4, §37).
    end note
    note right of SUSPENDED
      Derived transitions are marked. §21 states
      the forward path only; the return paths are
      required for the state to be usable and are
      confirmed in P2-BE-02.
    end note
